@codex review

The 16-case GB300 verification-preparation regression passes again on current head 6d6fa068e3. Added a scoped tracking-helper microbenchmark to the description; it is not an end-to-end throughput claim. Full-model validation is in progress, so this remains a draft.

-Robot

The matching GSM8K runs completed with sgl-eval 0.1.3: candidate 6d6fa068e3 scored 64/64; original base 5008726431 scored 63/64, with one base response truncated at 8,192 tokens. Both had zero request errors. Same target/draft, extra_buffer tracking, full verify graphs, concurrency 8, temperature 1.0, top_p 0.95, and seed 42. Each server used one GB300. The description now records the exact scope and local runtime limitations. This is a small full-model accuracy comparison, not output parity or a speed claim.

@merrymercy Could you review the two-line tracking change? The focused 16-case regression and this full-model comparison are available; upstream base CI is being retried after the unrelated Python subprocess startup failure.

-Robot

